WEBVTT

00:00:04.480 --> 00:00:09.780
There's always someone better, but for the best, it's all downhill.

00:00:20.500 --> 00:00:23.750
Day 4

00:00:36.930 --> 00:00:39.560
2nd Floor, Ibuki Kanami's Room

00:01:03.910 --> 00:01:06.830
Genius Engineer

00:01:07.840 --> 00:01:12.600
Well, we can't just leave her like this.

00:01:19.080 --> 00:01:20.560
Wait, Ii-chan.

00:01:21.000 --> 00:01:22.120
What? Why?

00:01:22.660 --> 00:01:24.680
Paint isn't dry yet.

00:01:28.700 --> 00:01:29.700
You're right.

00:01:30.040 --> 00:01:31.260
Hang on.

00:01:35.780 --> 00:01:37.820
Didn't that coat mean a lot to you?

00:01:38.200 --> 00:01:40.940
Not the time or place for that.

00:02:02.330 --> 00:02:09.480
What I lack is everything you have

00:02:09.720 --> 00:02:16.640
What I want to be is everything you want

00:02:17.060 --> 00:02:20.240
The moment we first met

00:02:20.700 --> 00:02:23.780
I'm sure I already knew

00:02:23.780 --> 00:02:28.120
Even before it began

00:02:28.120 --> 00:02:31.840
Behind my words

00:02:31.840 --> 00:02:34.840
I'm always hiding

00:02:34.840 --> 00:02:40.100
Keeping my feelings buried deep

00:02:40.100 --> 00:02:54.040
Now, the world that keeps us trapped sure changes before you know it

00:02:54.860 --> 00:03:03.220
I mean my heart's already dyed a single color,
in my mind the answer's already been chosen

00:03:03.220 --> 00:03:09.700
Is it fate? I don't know, but I'll reach out my hand

00:03:09.700 --> 00:03:13.380
I bet we don't need words at all

00:03:13.380 --> 00:03:17.260
Your melody and my rhythm

00:03:17.260 --> 00:03:21.860
Clamp up our feelings and spin out our fingers

00:03:21.860 --> 00:03:25.220
I'll always be right here

00:03:25.350 --> 00:03:31.100
<i>The Beheading Cycle</i>

00:03:25.350 --> 00:03:31.100
<i>The Blue Savant and
the Master of Nonsense</i>

00:03:25.600 --> 00:03:29.060
Right by your side

00:03:26.850 --> 00:03:31.100
<i>Day 4 (1) Beheading 1</i>

00:03:27.140 --> 00:03:31.100
<i>The Beheading Cycle</i>

00:03:31.980 --> 00:03:34.360
1st Floor, Dining Room

00:03:47.900 --> 00:03:53.320
I...well...after dinner, I was with Kunagisa the whole time.

00:03:54.180 --> 00:03:58.380
Then Kunagisa said she was hungry, so we went to the living room.

00:03:58.920 --> 00:04:02.620
Hikari and Maki and Shinya were in the living room, and...

00:04:02.940 --> 00:04:04.890
Then the earthquake.

00:04:06.420 --> 00:04:07.560
Everyone felt that?

00:04:08.600 --> 00:04:11.100
We were in the living room until the earthquake.

00:04:11.860 --> 00:04:14.440
Then I took Kunagisa back to her room...

00:04:15.100 --> 00:04:17.260
And then...I went to sleep.

00:04:18.200 --> 00:04:19.900
Hikari, is that true?

00:04:20.120 --> 00:04:22.840
Yes. The earthquake happened around...

00:04:23.720 --> 00:04:27.160
Um, one o'clock? Right?

00:04:27.460 --> 00:04:32.680
The five of us were talking in the living room then. I can vouch for that much.

00:04:33.120 --> 00:04:33.960
Okay.

00:04:35.200 --> 00:04:36.760
You and Kunagisa...

00:04:37.560 --> 00:04:39.180
Sakaki and Himena...

00:04:39.760 --> 00:04:40.740
...and Hikari.

00:04:41.120 --> 00:04:46.180
The five of you can provide each other alibis until the earthquake.

00:04:46.680 --> 00:04:48.220
What about after?

00:04:48.840 --> 00:04:52.520
I was asleep, alone in my room. I have no alibi.

00:04:52.520 --> 00:04:53.620
Thank you.

00:04:54.640 --> 00:05:00.580
Last night, I was in my room with Rei and Sashirono, talking.

00:05:01.360 --> 00:05:06.440
Last night's dinner was particularly magnificent,
and I simply had to know the recipe.

00:05:06.820 --> 00:05:08.440
Isn't that right, Sashirono?

00:05:09.500 --> 00:05:10.220
Yes.

00:05:12.220 --> 00:05:16.860
After the earthquake, I...went back to my room.

00:05:17.700 --> 00:05:18.960
That's right!

00:05:19.560 --> 00:05:23.180
Rei and I talked until morning.

00:05:23.840 --> 00:05:29.060
Since Kunagisa is leaving soon we hoped to think of
some grand entertainment for her last day.

00:05:29.060 --> 00:05:30.460
A good-bye party.

00:05:30.760 --> 00:05:31.720
As is our wont.

00:05:32.420 --> 00:05:37.980
We completely missed our chance to sleep,
so we decided to have breakfast first.

00:05:38.240 --> 00:05:41.980
Shinya and I have flawless alibis, at any rate.

00:05:42.620 --> 00:05:46.260
Kunagisa's already covered us until the earthquake...

00:05:46.260 --> 00:05:52.120
And after that, Shinya and I drank the rest of the night away.

00:05:52.300 --> 00:05:54.120
Ain't wine grand?

00:05:54.480 --> 00:05:58.300
How trustworthy is the testimony of a drunk?

00:06:02.000 --> 00:06:03.000
Right?

00:06:04.060 --> 00:06:04.660
Oh...

00:06:05.440 --> 00:06:06.960
Yes, that's true.

00:06:09.260 --> 00:06:12.500
Hikari? What did you do after the earthquake?

00:06:12.820 --> 00:06:17.020
I went back to our room. Akari and Teruko were there.

00:06:18.120 --> 00:06:21.620
I went to sleep. I woke at five, and started work...

00:06:21.800 --> 00:06:24.720
So Akari and Teruko? Akari, you answer.

00:06:25.300 --> 00:06:29.640
We had no further duties after dinner, so...

00:06:30.480 --> 00:06:33.160
So Teruko and I were in our room the whole time.

00:06:33.520 --> 00:06:39.660
After the earthquake, Hikari joined us, and we all went to sleep.

00:06:42.820 --> 00:06:45.680
What about you? How did you spend your evening?

00:06:47.340 --> 00:06:48.660
Yeah, well...

00:06:49.520 --> 00:06:52.440
I spent no time with anyone else.

00:06:55.720 --> 00:06:59.400
But just for the record, I'm not the killer.

00:06:59.960 --> 00:07:04.680
I do hate artists, but I don't even consider them worth killing.

00:07:07.080 --> 00:07:09.840
Still...yet another death.

00:07:10.740 --> 00:07:11.480
'Another'?

00:07:11.680 --> 00:07:13.680
And a beheading...!

00:07:14.320 --> 00:07:17.360
Is this island cursed!?

00:07:17.620 --> 00:07:20.920
Himena, could you please do a reading on that?

00:07:20.920 --> 00:07:23.000
You're the one who's cursed, Ilia.

00:07:23.360 --> 00:07:25.500
The island is just an island.

00:07:25.500 --> 00:07:28.760
If anyone here is cursed, it would have to be you.

00:07:29.000 --> 00:07:30.540
You have a point there!

00:07:33.340 --> 00:07:36.940
But this new case is a simple one.

00:07:36.940 --> 00:07:41.140
After all, we know the time of death.

00:07:41.280 --> 00:07:42.040
We do?

00:07:42.040 --> 00:07:42.880
We do.

00:07:43.380 --> 00:07:45.140
You saw it yourself.

00:07:45.140 --> 00:07:50.100
The earthquake knocked the paint over,
and Ibuki's body was on the other side.

00:07:50.760 --> 00:07:54.060
How wide was that paint river?

00:07:54.480 --> 00:07:57.280
At least three meters across.

00:07:57.680 --> 00:08:02.480
Yes. Not exactly easy to jump across, is it?

00:08:03.160 --> 00:08:08.420
Therefore, the case must have happened <i>before</i> the earthquake.

00:08:08.420 --> 00:08:09.760
That's not true!

00:08:10.560 --> 00:08:14.300
I'm afraid you've made a mistake there, Ilia.

00:08:14.900 --> 00:08:16.540
Oh? How so?

00:08:16.800 --> 00:08:21.040
C'mon, Ii-chan. Tell her. About last night.

00:08:21.860 --> 00:08:24.800
About last night...what about it?

00:08:26.220 --> 00:08:31.660
Argh, you really don't remember? How could
you forget something so important?

00:08:32.000 --> 00:08:33.960
Right after the earthquake!

00:08:34.260 --> 00:08:37.120
Shinya called Kanami!

00:08:39.940 --> 00:08:44.740
In other words, Kanami must have been killed after the earthquake.

00:08:44.900 --> 00:08:47.620
Wait...but the paint river...

00:08:47.800 --> 00:08:51.200
What that means, Ilia, is...

00:08:51.880 --> 00:08:55.320
The studio...was a locked room.

00:08:58.180 --> 00:09:01.520
Sakaki, are you absolutely sure it was Ibuki you spoke to?

00:09:02.280 --> 00:09:06.760
Yes, it was definitely her. I'm sure of it.

00:09:07.320 --> 00:09:12.980
She said she was working...and the paint had fallen over and made a mess.

00:09:13.960 --> 00:09:19.340
So I know...that she was still alive after the earthquake.

00:09:19.340 --> 00:09:22.880
Then this is a very strange story.

00:09:22.880 --> 00:09:26.180
The murder must have happened after the earthquake.

00:09:27.280 --> 00:09:30.580
But after the earthquake, there was a river of paint to cross.

00:09:31.340 --> 00:09:36.220
Which means nobody could possibly have killed her.

00:09:36.380 --> 00:09:40.720
Right, Akane! This is a very strange case.

00:09:40.980 --> 00:09:43.720
So that's what you meant by 'locked room'.

00:09:45.600 --> 00:09:49.360
The paint still wasn't dry this morning, right?

00:09:50.520 --> 00:09:56.100
Then anyone crossing the river to get into
the room would have left footprints.

00:09:59.020 --> 00:10:03.320
Akari вЂ“ where exactly is the intercom phone in Ibuki's studio?

00:10:03.580 --> 00:10:05.440
On the stand next to the windows.

00:10:07.700 --> 00:10:13.920
Kunagisa, if you've posed the problem, do you also have a solution?

00:10:14.700 --> 00:10:17.460
Do you know who did it?

00:10:17.640 --> 00:10:19.220
Not at all!

00:10:19.660 --> 00:10:24.980
What about the window? Is it possibly to get in that way?

00:10:25.600 --> 00:10:28.420
On the second floor? I don't think so.

00:10:29.000 --> 00:10:33.720
And the window was locked from the inside...

00:10:33.940 --> 00:10:37.240
There's no way to open it from the outside?

00:10:37.820 --> 00:10:38.640
Probably?

00:10:46.900 --> 00:10:52.000
Really? I thought we'd already moved beyond suspecting me.

00:10:52.160 --> 00:10:53.760
Not likely.

00:10:54.060 --> 00:10:59.420
After all, it's physically impossible to leap across that river.

00:10:59.760 --> 00:11:03.380
Therefore the crime must have happened before the earthquake.

00:11:03.640 --> 00:11:06.000
What about Shinya's phone call?

00:11:06.000 --> 00:11:09.880
There are other explanations. He might have been hearing things.

00:11:12.960 --> 00:11:18.420
I mean, I know Ibuki and I didn't exactly get along...

00:11:19.360 --> 00:11:25.680
Then what should we do? I am the prime suspect вЂ“ so be it.

00:11:25.680 --> 00:11:28.280
So what now?

00:11:30.200 --> 00:11:31.280
Good question.

00:11:33.180 --> 00:11:37.420
Turn me over to the police, if you like.

00:11:37.700 --> 00:11:40.940
I hate the police.

00:11:41.940 --> 00:11:43.680
There must be some other way...

00:11:44.340 --> 00:11:45.420
Hey, Tomo.

00:11:45.700 --> 00:11:47.080
What, Ii-chan?

00:11:47.600 --> 00:11:50.140
Is there a way to end this witch trial?

00:11:50.640 --> 00:11:51.300
There is.

00:11:51.500 --> 00:11:52.200
There is?

00:11:53.140 --> 00:11:54.440
There is, but...

00:11:55.100 --> 00:12:00.180
But I don't think it should come from me. You say it.

00:12:01.420 --> 00:12:02.360
Yeah, I know.

00:12:04.880 --> 00:12:05.840
Yes? You.

00:12:06.520 --> 00:12:07.660
I have a suggestion.

00:12:08.140 --> 00:12:08.880
What is it?

00:12:09.500 --> 00:12:16.980
The room I'm using...if I'm right, the lock on it
can only be opened from the outside.

00:12:16.960 --> 00:12:18.090
1st Floor, Storeroom

00:12:18.480 --> 00:12:21.580
What if we put Akane there for safekeeping?

00:12:22.280 --> 00:12:26.020
Safekeeping? Sure you're not just locking me up?

00:12:26.460 --> 00:12:30.380
Absolutely not. This is not a prison, not a punishment.

00:12:31.380 --> 00:12:33.520
Simply a separation.

00:12:34.880 --> 00:12:42.080
Ilia, what I fear most is this case leading to another murder.

00:12:42.900 --> 00:12:47.860
The easiest way of preventing that is to
separate the primary suspect from the rest of us.

00:12:48.220 --> 00:12:51.960
If Akane is the killer, than nobody else will die.

00:12:52.740 --> 00:13:00.380
If someone else is the killer, someone who used
some sort of trick to kill Kanami after the earthquake...

00:13:00.740 --> 00:13:10.060
Then that person will be prevented from taking any further action.
If they take further action, that will prove that Akane was innocent.

00:13:10.960 --> 00:13:13.060
In other words, we create a stalemate.

00:13:14.240 --> 00:13:17.760
Make it so the killer can't do anything else.

00:13:18.320 --> 00:13:20.560
I see. That makes sense!

00:13:21.400 --> 00:13:24.780
But we can't keep her locked in there forever, you know.

00:13:25.200 --> 00:13:27.280
Just until the police get here.

00:13:28.200 --> 00:13:32.500
This island might be isolated, but give them a day or two and...

00:13:32.500 --> 00:13:33.900
There will be no police.

00:13:34.900 --> 00:13:36.420
I mean, think about it.

00:13:36.780 --> 00:13:40.560
There is absolutely nothing to be gained from their involvement.

00:13:41.060 --> 00:13:44.680
They will simply assume that Sonoyama was the killer.

00:13:45.060 --> 00:13:47.440
They won't do anything worth doing.

00:13:47.440 --> 00:13:49.900
But...we can't <i>not</i> call them.

00:13:50.560 --> 00:13:53.240
If we don't, the plan doesn't work.

00:13:53.240 --> 00:13:56.700
Well, then we'll just have to solve the case ourselves.

00:13:57.520 --> 00:13:59.700
Are you going to solve it?

00:14:00.000 --> 00:14:04.280
Have you forgotten? I mentioned it yesterday. In one week...

00:14:04.980 --> 00:14:06.440
Only six days, now.

00:14:07.040 --> 00:14:12.260
The most talented mind is gracing us with a visit.

00:14:13.280 --> 00:14:18.960
I am sure Aikawa will settle this matter within an inch of its life.

00:14:19.680 --> 00:14:20.920
Six days...

00:14:22.400 --> 00:14:29.380
Very well. If accepting this confinement
improves the situation, then I have no choice.

00:14:30.600 --> 00:14:34.600
Ilia, we can trust this Aikawa?

00:14:34.980 --> 00:14:36.720
Yes. Absolutely.

00:14:39.820 --> 00:14:42.040
Then lead the way.

00:14:46.740 --> 00:14:49.490
2nd Floor, Kunagisa Tomo's Room

00:14:49.900 --> 00:14:52.360
Was this really the best choice?

00:14:52.580 --> 00:14:54.460
I think so.

00:14:54.460 --> 00:14:57.880
You said more or less what I was thinking.

00:14:57.880 --> 00:15:00.240
I bet Akane's grateful, too.

00:15:00.800 --> 00:15:06.000
It's a lot better than arguing forever, anyway.

00:15:06.740 --> 00:15:07.840
I hope so.

00:15:11.580 --> 00:15:12.500
Done.

00:15:12.820 --> 00:15:14.340
Thank you!

00:15:18.220 --> 00:15:22.100
I just feel like I've done her wrong.

00:15:22.480 --> 00:15:27.820
I can see why. But you did what needed to be done, Ii-chan.

00:15:33.100 --> 00:15:34.080
Hey, Tomo.

00:15:34.080 --> 00:15:35.460
Yes, Ii-chan?

00:15:35.460 --> 00:15:36.340
Do me a favor.

00:15:36.860 --> 00:15:38.380
Anything. What?

00:15:39.060 --> 00:15:41.640
Can you do something about the locked room?

00:15:42.280 --> 00:15:48.480
I'm not sure I can, but as a favor to you, I'll certainly try!

00:15:49.860 --> 00:15:53.140
Tomo, do you think Akane did it?

00:15:53.740 --> 00:15:55.560
I wouldn't say that.

00:15:56.080 --> 00:15:59.420
Akane's right вЂ“ there is no proof.

00:15:59.820 --> 00:16:03.060
The process of elimination isn't enough.

00:16:03.060 --> 00:16:05.880
We haven't even done an autopsy on the body.

00:16:06.620 --> 00:16:09.860
OK. So we're back to the locked room.

00:16:10.540 --> 00:16:16.820
Since the room was 'locked', nobody could have done it. Including Akane.

00:16:17.360 --> 00:16:20.280
You see any way past that, Ii-chan?

00:16:20.540 --> 00:16:21.400
I might.

00:16:22.220 --> 00:16:24.660
If I think on it a bit more an idea might strike me.

00:16:25.340 --> 00:16:28.660
You, Tomo? Any thoughts?

00:16:29.000 --> 00:16:30.020
Too many!

00:16:30.360 --> 00:16:33.680
If I think on it a bit more I might narrow it down.

00:16:34.360 --> 00:16:39.180
And then there's the headless corpse problem, Ii-chan.

00:16:39.660 --> 00:16:43.960
Normally, with headless bodies, you have
to look out for people switching places.

00:16:44.320 --> 00:16:47.620
In this case we can probably rule that out.

00:16:48.640 --> 00:16:52.860
There were twelve of us, and one beheaded, leaving eleven.

00:16:53.640 --> 00:16:56.700
And all eleven of us are present and accounted for.

00:16:58.320 --> 00:17:04.340
If one of the triplet maids had been killed,
then mistaken identity could have been a big problem.

00:17:04.940 --> 00:17:09.480
But I doubt we need to worry about it with Kanami.

00:17:09.780 --> 00:17:16.460
If we start considering accomplices and tricks to kill from
a distance, then the only people we can rule out right now...

00:17:16.760 --> 00:17:20.400
Are you and me.

00:17:20.960 --> 00:17:24.140
I get taking yourself off, but why me?

00:17:24.760 --> 00:17:25.800
I trust you.

00:17:31.200 --> 00:17:33.840
Still, a headless corpse!?

00:17:34.440 --> 00:17:37.660
No reason to behead someone except switching places!

00:17:38.620 --> 00:17:39.740
Or is there?

00:17:40.180 --> 00:17:41.680
We don't know the motive.

00:17:42.300 --> 00:17:45.340
Why did Kanami have to die?

00:17:45.740 --> 00:17:49.700
There's no reason why anyone should have to die.

00:17:50.800 --> 00:17:53.620
But I agree. Why'd this happen?

00:17:54.260 --> 00:17:59.940
Shinya was the only person who'd ever met Kanami before they came here.

00:18:00.780 --> 00:18:07.760
Or maybe not. I suppose we shouldn't rule out
the possibility of prior association.

00:18:08.540 --> 00:18:11.140
We'll keep it in mind.

00:18:12.220 --> 00:18:14.700
Okay, enough thinking!

00:18:15.260 --> 00:18:18.400
We can follow up on that stuff later.

00:18:18.800 --> 00:18:19.740
How?

00:18:19.940 --> 00:18:22.400
Who do you think I am?

00:18:23.640 --> 00:18:26.840
Then let's check the scene of the crime.

00:18:27.410 --> 00:18:31.040
2nd Floor, Hall

00:18:44.060 --> 00:18:45.260
What's she up to?

00:18:45.880 --> 00:18:48.300
Never seen Yayoi look like that!

00:18:48.740 --> 00:18:50.580
Something's bothering her...

00:18:51.300 --> 00:18:53.920
She seemed preoccupied with something, anyway.

00:18:56.640 --> 00:19:01.820
Coming from that direction, she might have been looking at Kanami's room.

00:19:02.200 --> 00:19:09.080
Same as us, trying to solve the mystery so she can go home.

00:19:09.400 --> 00:19:12.460
I dunno about that. She's been here longer than anybody.

00:19:12.860 --> 00:19:15.940
I'm not sure she'd be ready to leave that easily.

00:19:16.360 --> 00:19:20.840
Nothing like a murder to make you think about leaving places.

00:19:21.340 --> 00:19:23.480
Fair point.

00:19:23.780 --> 00:19:27.080
Not that it matters either way.

00:19:27.080 --> 00:19:32.000
If Yayoi solves the mystery, that's absolutely fine with me.

00:19:32.380 --> 00:19:34.840
Didn't look like there was much hope of that.

00:19:36.140 --> 00:19:37.360
She seemed...depressed.

00:19:37.760 --> 00:19:40.420
Downright melancholy.

00:19:40.960 --> 00:19:44.500
I'd be more ready to believe she'd just been destroying evidence.

00:19:44.680 --> 00:19:46.640
That would be bad!

00:19:46.640 --> 00:19:49.380
We'd better be quick, Ii-chan!

00:19:54.460 --> 00:19:55.440
Hunh.

00:19:58.000 --> 00:20:00.640
How much was that coat?

00:20:01.160 --> 00:20:03.980
Got two of them for around 10,000.

00:20:04.600 --> 00:20:05.320
Dollars?

00:20:06.520 --> 00:20:07.040
Yen.

00:20:10.940 --> 00:20:14.580
Well, we'd better go in.

00:20:29.260 --> 00:20:30.380
Hey, Tomo.

00:20:30.380 --> 00:20:31.080
What?

00:20:31.580 --> 00:20:33.460
This painting seem odd to you?

00:20:34.320 --> 00:20:36.660
You meet the painting of you?

00:20:37.700 --> 00:20:39.580
What? Looks normal to me.

00:20:40.220 --> 00:20:42.940
Grab a shot of it, please. Something's bugging me.

00:20:43.520 --> 00:20:44.420
Got it.

00:20:49.160 --> 00:20:52.320
Don't really see anything interesting on this end.

00:20:52.840 --> 00:20:57.820
Oh yeah, where is the head? The killer took it with them?

00:20:58.160 --> 00:21:01.080
Where'd they put it?

00:21:01.380 --> 00:21:05.540
Half the island is forest and mountains. Probably buried it somewhere.

00:21:05.540 --> 00:21:10.720
Or tossed it in the ocean. Didn't lack for options, anyway.

00:21:11.080 --> 00:21:16.140
Which brings us back to why they cut the head off in the first place.

00:21:16.700 --> 00:21:21.340
I gotta another question. Look here, at the stump!

00:21:22.620 --> 00:21:26.480
It was cut off right at the base. Why'd they do that?

00:21:27.040 --> 00:21:32.880
Usually you go to chop off a head, you go
here, like in the middle of the neck.

00:21:38.160 --> 00:21:40.360
Nothing weird here, either.

00:21:40.640 --> 00:21:42.120
You think there would be?

00:21:43.200 --> 00:21:50.380
I thought someone might have messed with the
circuit to send an incoming call to another room.

00:21:51.320 --> 00:21:55.400
But since we can call out just fine, we can rule that out.

00:21:55.840 --> 00:21:58.040
No signs of tampering, either.

00:21:58.900 --> 00:21:59.880
The phone call...

00:22:01.720 --> 00:22:07.120
What was it again? When Shinya called here, what did Kanami say?

00:22:07.380 --> 00:22:11.120
The paint fell over, and she was working, so he shouldn't interrupt.

00:22:13.160 --> 00:22:21.900
If only Shinya had ignored her and gone to check anyway. Not to be mean...

00:22:22.240 --> 00:22:24.720
But he was her assistant. It's his job.

00:22:25.960 --> 00:22:28.420
You're probably right.

00:22:29.220 --> 00:22:31.820
But what's done is done.

00:22:35.340 --> 00:22:40.060
Is it possible they put the phone back the way it was afterwards?

00:22:41.220 --> 00:22:45.740
It's not impossible. But not really practical.

00:22:45.740 --> 00:22:49.360
Not like you can just plug it back in.

00:22:49.780 --> 00:22:50.620
Right.

00:22:51.920 --> 00:22:56.680
Then let's rule it out for now.

00:22:57.160 --> 00:23:00.200
Although that leaves us with a locked room.

00:23:00.200 --> 00:23:02.280
Do you think I'm lying?

00:23:03.980 --> 00:23:08.800
I heard her voice. I swear it was her.

00:23:11.620 --> 00:23:15.460
I'm not saying you're lying.

00:23:16.180 --> 00:23:18.340
I've got no reason to doubt your word.

00:23:19.080 --> 00:23:27.600
But...Shinya, just supposing вЂ“ hypothetically speaking вЂ“
is there any chance it wasn't Kanami on the phone?

00:23:27.600 --> 00:23:28.140
None.

00:23:29.060 --> 00:23:31.280
I've known her too long.

00:23:31.940 --> 00:23:35.860
Anyone else, maybe they could have been fooled, but not me.

00:23:36.600 --> 00:23:38.680
Am I...a suspect here?

00:23:39.360 --> 00:23:41.220
Not especially.

00:23:41.540 --> 00:23:45.360
Don't see that you had any reason to kill her.

00:23:46.080 --> 00:23:49.800
Do you know that? There might be more to me than you think.

00:23:55.380 --> 00:23:58.860
We can't just leave her like this.

00:24:02.760 --> 00:24:03.720
I'll help.

00:24:38.700 --> 00:24:41.540
Should we really have buried her?

00:24:41.860 --> 00:24:46.560
Why not? Shinya's the closest thing to family she has, he said.

00:24:46.560 --> 00:24:48.880
If he wants to bury her...

00:24:49.680 --> 00:24:54.360
We can't leave her in the studio for a week.

00:24:55.120 --> 00:24:57.500
You're not wrong there!

00:25:00.220 --> 00:25:04.680
By the way, Tomo, what's the penalty for improper disposal of a body?

00:25:04.940 --> 00:25:11.100
Maximum of three years. Plus additional charges
as applicable. Sentence would be suspended, though.

00:25:11.640 --> 00:25:15.840
And we're both minors, so don't worry.

00:25:16.300 --> 00:25:20.540
Pour enough money in I can get us both off scott free!

00:25:23.420 --> 00:25:24.700
Nonsense.

00:25:33.910 --> 00:25:39.370
The shape of the world I'd believed in

00:25:39.370 --> 00:25:42.790
Spun around when near you

00:25:42.960 --> 00:25:46.170
Leaning towards your right

00:25:46.170 --> 00:25:48.630
What I've got in my hands

00:25:48.630 --> 00:25:51.510
Is not a dream or nothing

00:25:51.510 --> 00:25:55.180
But there's something somewhere

00:25:55.180 --> 00:25:58.220
Throbbing in my heart

00:25:58.220 --> 00:26:01.140
If the one that you do love

00:26:01.140 --> 00:26:05.480
Agrees to put his arms around you

00:26:05.480 --> 00:26:08.230
Then what was a nebulous hope

00:26:08.230 --> 00:26:12.490
Shatters everything that kept you stable

00:26:12.490 --> 00:26:15.070
We'd once been so hollow

00:26:15.070 --> 00:26:17.910
Trapped inside that little box

00:26:17.910 --> 00:26:21.410
But now we've seen outside that box

00:26:21.410 --> 00:26:24.670
And have no idea where we are.

00:26:25.080 --> 00:26:26.500
That's all.

00:26:40.390 --> 00:26:42.890
Afterimages of our bliss

00:26:42.890 --> 00:26:45.730
Glimpses of the future

00:26:45.730 --> 00:26:49.320
A glance at something fragile

00:26:49.320 --> 00:26:54.160
Those times that we can still laugh together
